# Commits ignored by `git blame`.
#
# Repository-wide mechanical changes go here: module path renames, symbol
# renames, formatting sweeps and language sweeps. They touch hundreds of files
# without changing behaviour, so leaving them in `git blame` hides the commit
# that actually introduced a line.
#
# Enable locally (GitHub applies this file automatically):
#
#   git config blame.ignoreRevsFile .git-blame-ignore-revs
#
# One full 40-character hash per line, with a comment naming the change. The
# hash is only known after the rename is committed, so entries are added in a
# follow-up commit.
#
# Stage 0 "System name": the Go module path moved to
# github.com/GoatWhistle/timeline, the Timeline screen was renamed to Schedule,
# and the product was renamed to Timeline.
